// `say` is a statement keyword, so `@game.say(…)` used to parse as `@game.` plus a
// stray `say "…"` — the capability call vanished and the string went to stdout via
// println instead. The narration must reach the game's message queue, which is the
// difference this case measures.
! @game.register_room(#hall, ⟨name: "Hall", desc: "A hall."⟩)
! @game.start(#hall)
! @game.say("A bell rings.")
^ contains(@game.messages(), "A bell rings.")
